{"id":"f089e42e052ee73d328bad66f17a873df789be1f","axis":"silent","repo":"quarkusio/quarkus","sha":"f089e42e052ee73d328bad66f17a873df789be1f","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/src/main/asciidoc/security-openid-connect-client-reference.adoc","lines":["@@ -1009,6 +1009,7 @@ Providers might also restrict how many times a refresh token can be used."," "," `OidcClientRequestReactiveFilter`, `OidcClientRequestFilter`, `TokenProvider`, and `Tokens` producers always cache the tokens they acquire with the configured grant."," Tokens acquired with additional grant parameters, for example, with `tokenProvider.getAccessToken(Map.of(\"scope\", \"openid\"))` or by a custom filter, are cached per set of such parameters, because the parameters, for example, a requested `scope` or a subject token which has to be exchanged, can affect which tokens are issued.","+The token propagation filters, `AccessTokenRequestReactiveFilter` and `AccessTokenRequestFilter`, cache the tokens they exchange the same way, with the incoming access token being the additional grant parameter, see <<token-propagation-rest>> and <<token-propagation-resteasy>>."," By default, each filter and each token producer caches the tokens of up to 15 sets of additional grant parameters."," This limit is approximate, the cache can briefly exceed it when tokens are requested concurrently."," When the limit is reached, the tokens which are least likely to be needed again, for example, expired or least recently used tokens, are evicted.","@@ -1020,6 +1021,8 @@ Use the `quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size` property to change the limit"," quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size=30"," ----"," ","+Set this property to `0` to not cache the tokens acquired with additional grant parameters at all.","+"," [[revoke-access-tokens]]"," === Revoking access tokens"," ","@@ -1760,6 +1763,18 @@ quarkus.resteasy-client-oidc-token-propagation.exchange-token=true"," `AccessTokenRequestReactiveFilter` uses a default `OidcClient` by default."," A named `OidcClient` can be selected with a `quarkus.rest-client-oidc-token-propagation.client-name` configuration property or with the `io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.common.AccessToken#exchangeTokenClient` annotation attribute."," ","+`AccessTokenRequestReactiveFilter` caches the exchanged tokens, see <<additional-grant-parameters-token-cache>>, also when the token exchange is activated with the `io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.common.AccessToken#exchangeTokenClient` annotation attribute.","+An incoming access token is exchanged once and the exchanged token is propagated until it expires, even if the incoming access token is revoked in the meantime.","+By default, the exchanged tokens of up to 15 incoming access tokens are cached.","+Use the `quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size` property of the `OidcClient` which exchanges the tokens to change this limit, for example, when the tokens of many users are exchanged at the same time:","+","+[source,properties]","+----","+quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size=50","+----","+","+Set this property to `0` to exchange the incoming access token on every request, so that the OpenID Connect provider verifies the incoming access token every time and rejects it as soon as it is revoked.","+"," "," [[token-propagation-resteasy]]"," == Token Propagation for RESTEasy Classic","@@ -1889,6 +1904,18 @@ NOTE: `AccessTokenRequestFilter` will use `OidcClient` to exchange the current t"," `AccessTokenRequestFilter` uses a default `OidcClient` by default."," A named `OidcClient` can be selected with the `quarkus.resteasy-client-oidc-token-propagation.client-name` configuration property."," ","+`AccessTokenRequestFilter` caches the exchanged tokens, see <<additional-grant-parameters-token-cache>>, also when the token exchange is activated with the `io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.common.AccessToken#exchangeTokenClient` annotation attribute.","+An incoming access token is exchanged once and the exchanged token is propagated until it expires, even if the incoming access token is revoked in the meantime.","+By default, the exchanged tokens of up to 15 incoming access tokens are cached.","+Use the `quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size` property of the `OidcClient` which exchanges the tokens to change this limit, for example, when the tokens of many users are exchanged at the same time:","+","+[source,properties]","+----","+quarkus.oidc-client.token-cache-max-size=50","+----","+","+Set this property to `0` to exchange the incoming access token on every request, so that the OpenID Connect provider verifies the incoming access token every time and rejects it as soon as it is revoked.","+"," === RestClient JsonWebTokenRequestFilter"," "," Using `JsonWebTokenRequestFilter` is recommended if you work with Bearer JWT tokens whose claims, such as `issuer` and `audience`, can be modified and the updated tokens re-secured, for example, re-signed."],"additions":27,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-client/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/client/runtime/OidcClientConfig.java","lines":["@@ -194,10 +194,11 @@ public String getGrantType() {","     Optional<Duration> refreshInterval();"," ","     /**","-     * Maximum number of sets of additional grant parameters for which an OIDC client filter or a token producer,","-     * such as {@code TokenProvider}, caches the tokens.","+     * Maximum number of sets of additional grant parameters for which an OIDC client filter, an OIDC token propagation","+     * filter which exchanges tokens, or a token producer, such as {@code TokenProvider}, caches the tokens.","      * Tokens requested with additional grant parameters, for example, with different scopes or subject tokens","      * passed to {@code TokenProvider#getAccessToken(Map)}, are cached per set of parameters.","+     * Set this property to {@code 0} to not cache such tokens at all.","      * This number is approximate, the cache can briefly exceed it when tokens are requested concurrently.","      * This property is not relevant when tokens are acquired with the configured grant only, without additional","      * grant parameters, because such tokens are always cached."],"additions":3,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-client/runtime/src/main/java/io/quarkus/oidc/client/runtime/TokensHelper.java","lines":["@@ -46,9 +46,9 @@ public TokensHelper() {","     }"," ","     public TokensHelper(int tokenCacheMaxSize) {","-        if (tokenCacheMaxSize < 1) {","+        if (tokenCacheMaxSize < 0) {","             throw new IllegalArgumentException(","-                    \"The maximum number of sets of additional parameters the tokens are cached for must be at least 1\");","+                    \"The maximum number of sets of additional parameters the tokens are cached for must not be negative\");","         }","         this.tokenCacheMaxSize = tokenCacheMaxSize;","     }","@@ -147,6 +147,10 @@ private TokenRequestStateHolder tokenRequestStateHolder(Map<String, String> addi","             return noParametersHolder;","         }","         Map<String, String> key = Map.copyOf(additionalParameters);","+        if (tokenCacheMaxSize == 0) {","+            // the tokens acquired with additional parameters are not cached, each request manages its own state","+            return new TokenRequestStateHolder(key);","+        }","         TokenRequestStateHolder holder = tokenRequestStateHolders.get(key);","         if (holder != null) {","             holder.lastAccessed = System.nanoTime();"],"additions":6,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-client/runtime/src/test/java/io/quarkus/oidc/client/runtime/TokensHelperTest.java","lines":["@@ -502,8 +502,34 @@ void testFailedRequestWithoutParametersIsRepeatedByNextCall() {","     }"," ","     @Test","-    void testTokenCacheMaxSizeMustBePositive() {","-        assertThatThrownBy(() -> new TokensHelper(0)).isInstanceOf(IllegalArgumentException.class);","+    void testTokenCacheMaxSizeMustNotBeNegative() {","+        assertThatThrownBy(() -> new TokensHelper(-1)).isInstanceOf(IllegalArgumentException.class);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testTokensWithParametersAreNotCachedWhenCacheIsDisabled() {","+        helper = new TokensHelper(0);","+        assertIssuedFor(getTokens(SCOPE_A), SCOPE_A);","+        assertIssuedFor(getTokens(SCOPE_A), SCOPE_A);","+        assertThat(client.requests()).hasSize(2);","+        assertThat(client.requests()).allMatch(InMemoryOidcTestClient.Call::isGrant);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testTokensWithoutParametersAreCachedWhenCacheIsDisabled() {","+        helper = new TokensHelper(0);","+        Tokens first = getTokens(NO_PARAMS);","+        Tokens second = getTokens(NO_PARAMS);","+        assertThat(second.getAccessToken()).isEqualTo(first.getAccessToken());","+        assertThat(client.requests()).hasSize(1);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testInitTokensWithParametersDoesNotPrePopulateCacheWhenCacheIsDisabled() {","+        helper = new TokensHelper(0);","+        helper.initTokens(client, SCOPE_A);","+        assertIssuedFor(getTokens(SCOPE_A), SCOPE_A);","+        assertThat(client.requests()).hasSize(2);","     }"," ","     @Test"],"additions":28,"deletions":2,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-token-propagation-reactive/deployment/pom.xml","lines":["@@ -59,6 +59,11 @@","             <artifactId>rest-assured</artifactId>","             <scope>test</scope>","         </dependency>","+        <dependency>","+            <groupId>org.assertj</groupId>","+            <artifactId>assertj-core</artifactId>","+            <scope>test</scope>","+        </dependency>","         <dependency>","             <groupId>org.htmlunit</groupId>","             <artifactId>htmlunit</artifactId>"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-token-propagation-reactive/deployment/src/test/java/io/quarkus/oidc/token/propagation/reactive/deployment/test/ExchangedTokenCacheTest.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,236 @@","+package io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.reactive.deployment.test;","+","+import static org.assertj.core.api.Assertions.assertThat;","+import static org.awaitility.Awaitility.await;","+import static org.hamcrest.Matchers.equalTo;","+","+import java.time.Duration;","+import java.util.Set;","+","+import jakarta.inject.Inject;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.GET;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.Path;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.QueryParam;","+","+import org.eclipse.microprofile.rest.client.inject.RegisterRestClient;","+import org.eclipse.microprofile.rest.client.inject.RestClient;","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;","+import org.junit.jupiter.api.extension.RegisterExtension;","+","+import io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.common.AccessToken;","+import io.quarkus.security.Authenticated;","+import io.quarkus.test.QuarkusExtensionTest;","+import io.quarkus.test.common.QuarkusTestResource;","+import io.quarkus.test.oidc.server.OidcWiremockTestResource;","+import io.restassured.RestAssured;","+","+@QuarkusTestResource(OidcWiremockTestResource.class)","+class ExchangedTokenCacheTest {","+","+    private static final String DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT = \"default\";","+    private static final String SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT = \"small-cache\";","+    private static final String NO_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT = \"no-cache\";","+","+    @RegisterExtension","+    static final QuarkusExtensionTest test = new QuarkusExtensionTest()","+            .withApplicationRoot(jar -> jar","+                    .addClasses(Frontend.class, ProtectedResource.class, MockTokenEndpoint.class,","+                            DefaultOidcClientService.class, SmallCacheOidcClientService.class,","+                            NoCacheOidcClientService.class))","+            .withConfiguration(","+                    \"\"\"","+                            quarkus.oidc.auth-server-url=${keycloak.url:replaced-by-tests}/realms/quarkus","+                            quarkus.oidc.client-id=quarkus-app","+                            quarkus.oidc.credentials.secret=secret","+                            quarkus.oidc.application-type=hybrid","+                            quarkus.oidc.token.audience=any","+","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.auth-server-url=${quarkus.oidc.auth-server-url}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.client-id=${quarkus.oidc.client-id}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.credentials.client-secret.value=${quarkus.oidc.credentials.secret}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.credentials.client-secret.method=post","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.grant.type=exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.grant-options.exchange.audience=quarkus-app-exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.token-path=http://localhost:8081/mock-oidc/token","+","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.auth-server-url=${quarkus.oidc-client.auth-server-url}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.client-id=${quarkus.oidc-client.client-id}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.credentials.client-secret.value=${quarkus.oidc-client.credentials.client-secret.value}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.credentials.client-secret.method=post","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.grant.type=exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.grant-options.exchange.audience=quarkus-app-exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.token-path=${quarkus.oidc-client.token-path}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.small-cache.token-cache-max-size=2","+","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.auth-server-url=${quarkus.oidc-client.auth-server-url}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.client-id=${quarkus.oidc-client.client-id}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.credentials.client-secret.value=${quarkus.oidc-client.credentials.client-secret.value}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.credentials.client-secret.method=post","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.grant.type=exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.grant-options.exchange.audience=quarkus-app-exchange","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.token-path=${quarkus.oidc-client.token-path}","+                            quarkus.oidc-client.no-cache.token-cache-max-size=0","+","+                            quarkus.rest-client-oidc-token-propagation.exchange-token=true","+                            \"\"\");","+","+    @Inject","+    MockTokenEndpoint mockTokenEndpoint;","+","+    @Test","+    void testExchangedTokenIsReusedForSameIncomingToken() {","+        String token = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"same-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(token, \"bob\");","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(token)).isEqualTo(1);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testTokensAreExchangedPerIncomingToken() {","+        String firstToken = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"first-token\");","+        String secondToken = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"second-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(firstToken, \"bob\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(secondToken, \"carol\");","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, firstToken, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, secondToken, \"carol\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, firstToken, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, secondToken, \"carol\");","+","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(firstToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(secondToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testExpiredExchangedTokenIsExchangedAgain() {","+        String token = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"expiring-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(token, \"bob\", 2);","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(token)).isEqualTo(1);","+","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(token, \"carol\");","+        await().atMost(Duration.ofSeconds(10))","+                .untilAsserted(() -> assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"carol\"));","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(token)).isEqualTo(2);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testFailedExchangeIsNotCached() {","+        String token = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"failing-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithError(token);","+","+        RestAssured.given().auth().oauth2(token)","+                .queryParam(\"oidc-client\", DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT)","+                .when().get(\"/frontend/exchanged-user-name\")","+                .then()","+                .statusCode(500);","+","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(token, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(token)).isEqualTo(2);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testLeastRecentlyUsedExchangedTokenIsEvictedWhenCacheIsFull() {","+        String firstToken = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"first-cached-token\");","+        String secondToken = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"second-cached-token\");","+        String thirdToken = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"third-cached-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(firstToken, \"bob\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(secondToken, \"bob\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(thirdToken, \"bob\");","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, firstToken, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, secondToken, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, thirdToken, \"bob\");","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(firstToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(secondToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(thirdToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, thirdToken, \"bob\");","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(thirdToken)).isEqualTo(1);","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, firstToken, \"bob\");","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(firstToken)).isEqualTo(2);","+    }","+","+    @Test","+    void testTokenIsExchangedOnEveryRequestWhenCacheIsDisabled() {","+        String token = tokenIssuedToAlice(\"uncached-token\");","+        mockTokenEndpoint.respondWithTokenIssuedTo(token, \"bob\");","+","+        assertExchangedUserName(NO_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+        assertExchangedUserName(NO_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT, token, \"bob\");","+","+        assertThat(mockTokenEndpoint.exchangeCount(token)).isEqualTo(2);","+    }","+","+    private static String tokenIssuedToAlice(String subject) {","+        return OidcWiremockTestResource.generateJwtToken(\"alice\", Set.of(\"admin\"), subject);","+    }","+","+    private static void assertExchangedUserName(String oidcClient, String token, String userName) {","+        RestAssured.given().auth().oauth2(token)","+                .queryParam(\"oidc-client\", oidcClient)","+                .when().get(\"/frontend/exchanged-user-name\")","+                .then()","+                .statusCode(200)","+                .body(equalTo(userName));","+    }","+","+    @Path(\"/frontend\")","+    @Authenticated","+    public static class Frontend {","+","+        @Inject","+        @RestClient","+        DefaultOidcClientService defaultOidcClientService;","+","+        @Inject","+        @RestClient","+        SmallCacheOidcClientService smallCacheOidcClientService;","+","+        @Inject","+        @RestClient","+        NoCacheOidcClientService noCacheOidcClientService;","+","+        @GET","+        @Path(\"exchanged-user-name\")","+        public String exchangedUserName(@QueryParam(\"oidc-client\") String oidcClient) {","+            return switch (oidcClient) {","+                case DEFAULT_OIDC_CLIENT -> defaultOidcClientService.getUserName();","+                case SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT -> smallCacheOidcClientService.getUserName();","+                case NO_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT -> noCacheOidcClientService.getUserName();","+                default -> throw new IllegalArgumentException(\"Unknown OIDC client \" + oidcClient);","+            };","+        }","+    }","+","+    @RegisterRestClient(baseUri = \"http://localhost:8081/protected\")","+    @AccessToken","+    @Path(\"/\")","+    public interface DefaultOidcClientService {","+        @GET","+        String getUserName();","+    }","+","+    @RegisterRestClient(baseUri = \"http://localhost:8081/protected\")","+    @AccessToken(exchangeTokenClient = SMALL_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT)","+    @Path(\"/\")","+    public interface SmallCacheOidcClientService {","+        @GET","+        String getUserName();","+    }","+","+    @RegisterRestClient(baseUri = \"http://localhost:8081/protected\")","+    @AccessToken(exchangeTokenClient = NO_CACHE_OIDC_CLIENT)","+    @Path(\"/\")","+    public interface NoCacheOidcClientService {","+        @GET","+        String getUserName();","+    }","+}"],"additions":236,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"extensions/oidc-token-propagation-reactive/deployment/src/test/java/io/quarkus/oidc/token/propagation/reactive/deployment/test/MockTokenEndpoint.java","lines":["@@ -0,0 +1,66 @@","+package io.quarkus.oidc.token.propagation.reactive.deployment.test;","+","+import java.util.Map;","+import java.util.Set;","+import java.util.concurrent.ConcurrentHashMap;","+import java.util.concurrent.atomic.AtomicInteger;","+","+import jakarta.inject.Singleton;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.Consumes;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.FormParam;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.POST;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.Path;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.Produces;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.core.MediaType;","+import jakarta.ws.rs.core.Response;","+","+import io.quarkus.test.oidc.server.OidcWiremockTestResource;","+import io.vertx.core.json.JsonObject;","+","+/**","+ * Token endpoint which exchanges subject tokens for the tokens configured by the tests and counts the exchanges.","+ */","+@Singleton","+@Path(\"/mock-oidc/token\")","+public class MockTokenEndpoint {","+","+    private record TokenResponse(int status, String body) {","+    }","+","+    private final Map<String, TokenResponse> responses = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();","+    private final Map<String, AtomicInteger> exchanges = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();","+","+    @POST","+    @Consumes(MediaType.APPLICATION_FORM_URLENCODED)","+    @Produces(MediaType.APPLICATION_JSON)","+    public Response exchange(@FormParam(\"subject_token\") String subjectToken) {","+        exchanges.computeIfAbsent(subjectToken, t -> new AtomicInteger()).incrementAndGet();","+        TokenResponse response = responses.get(subjectToken);","+        if (response == null) {","+            throw new IllegalStateException(\"No response configured for the subject token \" + subjectToken);","+        }","+        return Response.status(response.status()).entity(response.body()).build();","+    }","+","+    void respondWithTokenIssuedTo(String subjectToken, String userName) {","+        responses.put(subjectToken, new TokenResponse(200, tokenJson(userName).encode()));","+    }","+","+    void respondWithTokenIssuedTo(String subjectT